Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/8925fd7b8239d5a7e7e5a26f8af306e006ab121a
From 8925fd7b8239d5a7e7e5a26f8af306e006ab121a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:26:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 47/48] avfilter: add the dibr filter

Depth-image-based rendering: a picture and its depth map become full
side by side, both views at the picture's size, the left eye first,
marked with Stereo 3D side data. libstereo-dibr does the work, the core
Sparky Stereo OS shares between FFmpeg, players and the desktop, and
every path of it is an option: the picture as the left eye or the
middle; forward, backward or layered warping; background extension,
depth-aided, Telea or no hole filling; an asymmetric Gaussian on the
depth or none.

What a depth sample means comes from the depth frame's side data: the
depth representation information of H.264 and H.265 (from the SEI
messages or an HEIF depth image), or the supplemental information of an
ISO/IEC 23002-3 auxiliary video stream, which is not freely available
and read as open implementations read it. Without either, larger
samples are nearer (2D-plus-depth), with a range and a screen plane as
options.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
